From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:17:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): recalled memory rides only its own turn

memory.recall_history (true = upstream behavior): with false, an external provider's <memory-context> block is sent with the turn it was recalled for only. Older turns lose it on the wire, in the session store (content and api_content) and in the summarizer's input; a pre_llm_call hook's context in the same row is kept. Each new turn then re-sends the previous turn once without prompt cache. memory.recall_max_chars (0 = no cap) cuts the middle of a long recall at line boundaries, keeping its first quarter and last three quarters (Honcho lists observations oldest first, then its peer card), and says where it cut.
